  501|      4|                // through the closure correctly. Otherwise, if we re-do the
  502|      4|                // epsilon closure needlessly, it could change based on the
  503|      4|                // fact that we are omitting epsilon states here.
  504|      4|                //
  505|      4|                // -----
  506|      4|                //
  507|      4|                // Welp, scratch the above. It turns out that recording these
  508|      4|                // is in fact necessary to seemingly handle one particularly
  509|      4|                // annoying case: when a conditional epsilon transition is
